# Everything ai/omopen produces is small (tens of kB), so the certificates,
# the per-class results and the canary file are all TRACKED -- they are the
# deliverable.  Only caches and scratch are ignored.
#
# Regeneration, in order (see OPEN_ATTACK.md section 8):
#   python gplib.py                       # identity tables + their self-test
#   python fpcheck.py --selftest
#   python attack.py enumerate
#   python validate.py --n 40
#   python canaries.py
#   python attack.py run --budget 60  --verify-identities
#   python attack.py run --budget 240 --walk-depth 60  --fp   # escalate
#   python attack.py run --budget 1800 --walk-depth 200 --fp   # if any remain
#   python attack.py witness
#   python attack.py report ; python table.py

__pycache__/
*.pyc
data/_*.jsonl
data/*.tmp

# scratch (the .md is the artifact of record; logs are ignored repo-wide)
data/_*

